WEBVTT

00:07.490 --> 00:09.480
<b>You must be the Oniwaban Group,
that you are.</b>

00:09.860 --> 00:12.280
<b>One of the famous Oniwaban Group.</b>

00:12.280 --> 00:14.990
<b>When they say Hyottoko, they mean me!</b>

00:15.160 --> 00:16.620
<b>Hyottoko?</b>

00:16.620 --> 00:18.620
<b>Sounds too cute to suit you.</b>

00:18.620 --> 00:19.830
<b>You should change your name.</b>

00:21.000 --> 00:23.330
<b>Quietly hand Megumi over.</b>

00:23.330 --> 00:26.290
<b>If you do, I'll go a little easy on you.</b>

00:26.790 --> 00:28.790
<b>Which one of you is up first?</b>

00:28.790 --> 00:31.630
<b>I don't care
if both of you come at me together.</b>

00:31.840 --> 00:34.550
<b>He boasts of massive strength
and fights with no weapon.</b>

00:35.050 --> 00:36.590
<b>Leave this one to me.</b>

00:36.840 --> 00:38.890
<b>However, we're up against
the Oniwaban Group.</b>

00:39.310 --> 00:41.560
<b>Who knows if that's all he is?</b>

00:41.560 --> 00:43.480
<b>I don't care! I'll nab him alive</b>

00:43.480 --> 00:45.520
<b>and force the truth
about the opium out of him!</b>

00:45.520 --> 00:47.650
<b>So you're up first.</b>

00:51.150 --> 00:54.990
<b>Even if you got the strength,
it means nothing if you can't hit with it.</b>

00:56.360 --> 00:58.030
<b>How gracious of you...</b>

00:58.410 --> 01:01.490
<b>to come into range for me.</b>

01:03.450 --> 01:04.790
<b>Sano!</b>

01:06.000 --> 01:07.080
<b>Wha—</b>

02:39.010 --> 02:43.010
<b>EPISODE 9: THE ONIWABANSHU STRIKE</b>

02:43.140 --> 02:43.970
<b>Sano!</b>

02:45.180 --> 02:46.060
<b>Wha—</b>

02:46.810 --> 02:47.640
<b>Sanosuke!</b>

02:53.190 --> 02:55.400
<b>That's dangerous, you putz!</b>

02:56.360 --> 03:01.200
<b>Oh? I'm surprised
you dodged my Flame Breath technique.</b>

03:01.200 --> 03:05.030
<b>However, you won't be able to dodge
the next one with that leg.</b>

03:08.080 --> 03:10.620
<b>He creates fire with sacks of oil
placed inside his stomach</b>

03:10.620 --> 03:12.460
<b>and teeth made of flint.</b>

03:12.460 --> 03:14.750
<b>The greatest fire master of the Oniwaban.</b>

03:15.000 --> 03:18.090
<b>His name "Hyottoko"
stems from "hi" and "otoko."</b>

03:18.090 --> 03:20.010
<b>There is nothing that he can't burn!</b>

03:24.430 --> 03:25.470
<b>Here goes.</b>

03:28.470 --> 03:30.060
<b>Why are you looking away?</b>

03:30.060 --> 03:32.140
<b>Your opponent is me, that I am.</b>

03:33.100 --> 03:35.480
<b>After I take care of him.</b>

03:35.650 --> 03:38.820
<b>Don't you fret. I'll burn you up next.</b>

03:39.030 --> 03:40.900
<b>A street performance like that</b>

03:40.900 --> 03:43.700
<b>won't be able to burn
one hair on me, that it won't.</b>

03:43.950 --> 03:46.870
<b>D-Did you call it a street performance?</b>

03:50.960 --> 03:54.290
<b>He sliced fire apart with his sakabato!</b>

03:59.000 --> 04:02.550
<b>Idiot! Don't think you can
defend everything with just one sword!</b>

04:05.800 --> 04:06.850
<b>Where are you off to?</b>

04:07.970 --> 04:11.020
<b>Kenshin is fighting for your sake.</b>

04:11.520 --> 04:14.350
<b>You should be properly
watching all of it happen.</b>

04:15.230 --> 04:17.400
<b>It's not an opponent
a swordsman can win against.</b>

04:17.900 --> 04:19.570
<b>He can buy some time,</b>

04:19.570 --> 04:22.240
<b>but he is facing the mid-ranking onmitsu
of the Oniwaban Group.</b>

04:22.650 --> 04:25.110
<b>He's nothing like Beshimi,
a low-level onmitsu.</b>

04:25.870 --> 04:26.870
<b>No, he will win!</b>

04:28.330 --> 04:30.120
<b>You know nothing about Kenshin.</b>

04:30.740 --> 04:34.170
<b>He may be a swordsman,
but he's no ordinary swordsman.</b>

04:36.420 --> 04:39.300
<b>Impossible. Nine liters of oil,
and I'm out?</b>

04:40.590 --> 04:41.960
<b>That's why I told you.</b>

04:42.510 --> 04:44.930
<b>You can't burn one hair on me.</b>

04:46.390 --> 04:49.010
<b>He defended against all the fire
with just a sword.</b>

04:49.430 --> 04:51.970
<b>Indeed, he is no ordinary swordsman!</b>

04:52.730 --> 04:54.770
<b>What in the world is he...</b>

04:57.400 --> 04:58.690
<b>Damn you.</b>

04:58.690 --> 05:00.610
<b>I'm not done yet!</b>

05:00.860 --> 05:02.490
<b>He's planning on replenishing his oil!</b>

05:04.490 --> 05:05.320
<b>Sano!</b>

05:05.780 --> 05:07.780
<b>Thanks for the help.</b>

05:08.200 --> 05:10.990
<b>But I'm the one dealing with him.</b>

05:11.740 --> 05:14.460
<b>Sorry, but I'm gonna reset this match!</b>

05:16.830 --> 05:19.920
<b>All right. I will leave you
with the rest, that I will.</b>

05:20.170 --> 05:22.130
<b>Yeah, leave this to me!</b>

05:22.130 --> 05:25.470
<b>Come on! Why are you guys
both acting tough?</b>

05:25.720 --> 05:27.590
<b>Replenishment complete.</b>

05:27.590 --> 05:32.770
<b>You are such a fool,
wandering over so you can be incinerated.</b>

05:32.770 --> 05:34.600
<b>No, you're the fool.</b>

05:35.480 --> 05:39.400
<b>You think a magic trick will work
over and over once the secret is out?</b>

05:40.480 --> 05:42.110
<b>I'll light you up!</b>

05:42.110 --> 05:45.840
<b>Any of you who call this technique,
my pride and joy,</b>

05:45.840 --> 05:50.120
<b>a street performance or a magic trick
are all gonna be cremated!</b>

05:51.280 --> 05:52.930
<b>Maximum Flame Breath!</b>

05:52.930 --> 05:54.700
<b>This time, you won't be able to dodge it!</b>

05:54.950 --> 05:57.460
<b>Give me a break!</b>

05:57.460 --> 05:58.210
<b>What?</b>

06:00.670 --> 06:02.340
<b>What a reckless guy.</b>

06:02.340 --> 06:05.550
<b>This truly is finding the way
out of a deadly situation, that it is.</b>

06:05.760 --> 06:08.380
<b>I'll take a look at the secret
behind your magic trick!</b>

06:10.340 --> 06:13.720
<b>For your pride and joy,
this is quite a dirty little secret.</b>

06:15.020 --> 06:17.100
<b>You have no chance of winning now.</b>

06:17.430 --> 06:19.190
<b>Just behave, and give up.</b>

06:20.560 --> 06:21.690
<b>Idiot.</b>

06:22.570 --> 06:25.320
<b>You're the one with no chance of winning!</b>

06:25.320 --> 06:29.740
<b>With that burnt arm, you won't
be able to punch like you did before!</b>

06:30.030 --> 06:34.240
<b>Eat my Flame Fist,
burning like a real flame!</b>

06:36.660 --> 06:39.500
<b>Kicks are totally legit
in a fight, you know?</b>

06:39.500 --> 06:43.670
<b>Though, with those short legs,
you'd never come up with that idea.</b>

06:48.220 --> 06:49.220
<b>Easy win!</b>

06:50.340 --> 06:53.430
<b>You say that,
but you're hurt all over, that you are.</b>

06:53.430 --> 06:54.890
<b>What was that?</b>

06:54.890 --> 06:59.390
<b>He won. All things said and done,
he really is strong.</b>

06:59.980 --> 07:02.730
<b>They're way beyond strong.</b>

07:02.730 --> 07:05.020
<b>What in the world are those two?</b>

07:05.020 --> 07:08.570
<b>I'm tellin' ya,
all that didn't need to be said!</b>

07:05.270 --> 07:07.690
<b>I told you. You don't know them.</b>

07:08.570 --> 07:11.360
<b>- There, there.
- Don't "there, there" me after all that!</b>

07:08.570 --> 07:12.450
<b>Those two are reliable comrades
one can be proud of.</b>

07:11.360 --> 07:13.870
<b>- Ha ha ha.
- Don't "ha ha ha" me!</b>

07:13.870 --> 07:15.240
<b>Hey, are you guys okay?</b>

07:16.290 --> 07:18.330
<b>You really are wounded all over.</b>

07:18.330 --> 07:20.080
<b>Looks like you won only by a little bit.</b>

07:20.370 --> 07:21.500
<b>Isn't that right, that is?</b>

07:21.500 --> 07:23.040
<b>What was that?</b>

07:23.420 --> 07:26.800
<b>That was an easy win,
no matter how you look at it! Damn it!</b>

07:23.830 --> 07:25.340
<b>- Come on.
- Oh, brother.</b>

07:25.340 --> 07:27.300
<b>Good grief. Oro?</b>

07:27.300 --> 07:28.380
<b><i>Friends.</i></b>

07:30.220 --> 07:32.510
<b>So what should we do with him?</b>

07:32.510 --> 07:35.350
<b>Let's see. We can splash water on him.</b>

07:37.180 --> 07:38.890
<b>Damn it. Damn it.</b>

07:38.890 --> 07:41.770
<b>Hyottoko let himself
be so easily defeated.</b>

07:41.980 --> 07:45.270
<b>This is gonna lead
to another failure for me.</b>

07:46.900 --> 07:47.730
<b>No.</b>

07:48.360 --> 07:50.610
<b>It's all because of Megumi Takani!</b>

07:50.610 --> 07:52.610
<b>If you didn't make a run for it
on my watch,</b>

07:52.610 --> 07:54.660
<b>this wouldn't have happened!</b>

07:54.660 --> 07:59.410
<b>The one that put me into this situation
ain't gonna get away with it unscathed!</b>

08:00.580 --> 08:01.660
<b>You're dead meat!</b>

08:02.410 --> 08:03.370
<b><i>Bloodlust!</i></b>

08:03.580 --> 08:06.210
<b>Be careful! Someone else is still lurking!</b>

08:06.750 --> 08:08.380
<b>- There you are!
- Die!</b>

08:11.550 --> 08:12.380
<b>Look out!</b>

08:13.760 --> 08:14.760
<b>What?</b>

08:15.800 --> 08:16.720
<b>Yahiko!</b>

08:17.050 --> 08:19.310
<b>Sheesh, you really are reckless!</b>

08:19.310 --> 08:20.470
<b>Ow.</b>

08:20.470 --> 08:22.430
<b>It's dangerous, so you should stand back!</b>

08:22.770 --> 08:24.440
<b>Give me a break!</b>

08:24.440 --> 08:28.270
<b>I don't really get it, but Kenshin and
Sanosuke are protecting this woman, right?</b>

08:28.520 --> 08:30.860
<b>I'm a part of Team Kenshin, too!</b>

08:30.860 --> 08:34.410
<b>Even if I can't go on the offensive, I can
properly do my job on the defensive end!</b>

08:34.950 --> 08:37.240
<b>You need to have more faith
in your students...</b>

08:39.990 --> 08:41.000
<b>Yahiko!</b>

08:41.870 --> 08:42.710
<b>Not good.</b>

08:43.580 --> 08:44.670
<b>Poison!</b>

08:46.040 --> 08:47.960
<b>That's what he gets
for sticking his nose in!</b>

08:47.960 --> 08:50.380
<b>That kid won't last an hour!</b>

08:50.840 --> 08:52.630
<b>Dokusatsu Rasenbyo!</b>

08:52.630 --> 08:56.720
<b>This is the true technique
of Beshimi of the Oniwaban Group!</b>

08:56.930 --> 08:58.930
<b>You're next, redhea...</b>

09:11.400 --> 09:12.690
<b><i>He's skilled.</i></b>

09:12.690 --> 09:13.900
<b>Kenshin!</b>

09:14.200 --> 09:16.320
<b>Yahiko... Yahiko is...</b>

09:16.530 --> 09:18.780
<b>Damn it, Yahiko, get a grip!</b>

09:19.240 --> 09:20.120
<b>Yahiko!</b>

09:20.830 --> 09:21.990
<b>Yahiko!</b>

09:23.080 --> 09:26.080
<b>RUROUNI KENSHIN</b>

09:29.790 --> 09:30.750
<b>Yahiko!</b>

09:36.590 --> 09:39.930
<b>Enough. Even with further combat,</b>

09:39.930 --> 09:42.560
<b>I sense it is impossible
for us to reclaim Megumi Takani.</b>

09:42.930 --> 09:46.570
<b>I myself want to pick up the two that fell</b>

09:46.570 --> 09:49.530
<b>and report to the leader
as soon as possible.</b>

09:49.770 --> 09:53.440
<b>You were the ones that attacked.
I won't hold you back.</b>

09:53.440 --> 09:57.990
<b>However, you will leave the little one
behind for Yahiko's detoxification.</b>

09:58.320 --> 10:00.950
<b>We have no duty
to go that far for enemies.</b>

10:01.280 --> 10:03.870
<b>Then I will have you leave him here
at any cost.</b>

10:06.750 --> 10:10.670
<b>You're quite passionate
for having such a collected demeanor.</b>

10:14.800 --> 10:16.260
<b>No need to fret.</b>

10:16.260 --> 10:20.260
<b>As long as you shelter Megumi Takani,
we will fight at some point.</b>

10:20.760 --> 10:23.260
<b>The showdown will be delayed until then.</b>

10:25.060 --> 10:29.350
<b><i>How he moves, that's a kenpo master
who has trained extensively!</i></b>

10:30.310 --> 10:32.060
<b>Kenshin! Yahiko is...</b>

10:32.610 --> 10:33.610
<b>Yahiko!</b>

10:35.650 --> 10:36.490
<b>How is he?</b>

10:37.110 --> 10:40.200
<b>I have experience treating
sword and spear cuts or broken bones,</b>

10:40.200 --> 10:41.700
<b>but detoxification...</b>

10:42.160 --> 10:44.830
<b>For now, we can suck out
the poison from the wound.</b>

10:44.830 --> 10:45.740
<b>Got it!</b>

10:45.740 --> 10:46.580
<b>Stop that.</b>

10:48.910 --> 10:51.130
<b>Are you telling me
to just watch Yahiko die?</b>

10:51.130 --> 10:52.130
<b>You stay out of this!</b>

10:52.130 --> 10:53.210
<b>You fool!</b>

10:53.210 --> 10:56.760
<b>Sucking poison out of a wound
can cause bacterial infections,</b>

10:56.760 --> 10:58.010
<b>so it makes things worse!</b>

10:58.420 --> 11:00.970
<b>This is no place for amateurs. Stand back!</b>

11:03.640 --> 11:05.680
<b><i>Slight fever, unconscious...</i></b>

11:05.680 --> 11:10.390
<b><i>slight pain, and most of all,
eye dilation. This is...</i></b>

11:10.730 --> 11:12.400
<b><i>stramonium leaf poison.</i></b>

11:12.900 --> 11:16.980
<b>Miss, this is a dojo, so you have
need of a regular doctor, don't you?</b>

11:17.150 --> 11:19.780
<b>I'll write out a list of medications,
so have him bring them!</b>

11:19.950 --> 11:23.450
<b>Ken-san, boil some water! And ready
some hand towels and household medicine!</b>

11:23.950 --> 11:26.950
<b>You, head to the ice store,
and buy all the ice they've got!</b>

11:27.290 --> 11:30.370
<b>Detoxification treatment
is a race against time! Hurry up!</b>

11:33.630 --> 11:35.840
<b>Hmph. That should do it.</b>

11:36.420 --> 11:39.550
<b>Three or four more days,
and he should recover.</b>

11:39.800 --> 11:42.550
<b>Good for you, Yahiko.</b>

11:42.550 --> 11:45.010
<b>That is, if he rests quietly.</b>

11:45.720 --> 11:47.390
<b>Thanks, old man.</b>

11:47.390 --> 11:49.350
<b>You're pretty amazing.</b>

11:49.350 --> 11:51.690
<b>That doesn't sound like thanks at all.</b>

11:52.020 --> 11:55.190
<b>And if you want to say thanks,
say it to whoever wrote this.</b>

11:55.440 --> 11:58.280
<b>Quite impressive.
A perfect note of ingredients</b>

11:58.280 --> 12:01.070
<b>and compounding instructions
for the antidote.</b>

12:01.860 --> 12:05.070
<b>Whoever wrote this is well-versed
in Dutch studies,</b>

12:05.070 --> 12:08.700
<b>what they call Western medicine nowadays.</b>

12:08.700 --> 12:12.120
<b>Maybe they just knew a lot about poison?</b>

12:12.120 --> 12:14.830
<b>It's a fine line
between poison and medicine.</b>

12:14.830 --> 12:19.000
<b>Stramonium leaves can be
wonderful medication, depending on usage.</b>

12:19.300 --> 12:25.220
<b>This was written by a master especially
versed in the drugs of Western medicine.</b>

12:25.430 --> 12:27.140
<b>I'm surprised.</b>

12:27.140 --> 12:29.930
<b>I thought she was
just a mean-spirited woman.</b>

12:30.140 --> 12:31.600
<b>A woman?</b>

12:31.600 --> 12:33.850
<b>Can it be Megumi Takani?</b>

12:34.690 --> 12:36.060
<b>You know her?</b>

12:36.560 --> 12:39.480
<b>Megumi Takani,
a girl who was the assistant</b>

12:39.480 --> 12:43.360
<b>for a certain doctor
who was murdered three years ago.</b>

12:49.030 --> 12:50.540
<b>Where are you going, that you are?</b>

12:51.500 --> 12:54.210
<b>It's dangerous for a woman
to walk around at night, that it is.</b>

12:54.620 --> 12:57.130
<b><i>This man keeps surprising me.</i></b>

12:58.420 --> 13:00.800
<b>Shouldn't you be at that boy's side?</b>

13:01.170 --> 13:05.720
<b>It's fine. Despite his looks, Yahiko
is quite a tenacious guy, that he is.</b>

13:06.180 --> 13:07.760
<b>Thank you for the treatment, that is.</b>

13:08.260 --> 13:10.560
<b>I will say thanks in Yahiko's place,
that I will.</b>

13:10.890 --> 13:12.770
<b>No need for thanks.</b>

13:12.770 --> 13:14.730
<b>Beshimi was targeting me, after all.</b>

13:15.480 --> 13:17.900
<b>So where are you headed to now,
that you are?</b>

13:18.400 --> 13:20.230
<b><i>And he doesn't let me change the topic.</i></b>

13:20.820 --> 13:22.650
<b>I'll be leaving Tokyo, for starters.</b>

13:23.150 --> 13:25.910
<b>This nuisance will be gone quickly,
so rest assured.</b>

13:26.410 --> 13:28.450
<b>So nobody back in your homeland of Aizu</b>

13:28.450 --> 13:30.660
<b>is waiting for your return,
that they aren't?</b>

13:31.990 --> 13:36.870
<b>Your word choice for "nuisance"
is that of someone from Aizu, is it not?</b>

13:37.290 --> 13:42.340
<b>I have fought against samurai from Aizu
countless times in Bakumatsu era Kyoto,</b>

13:42.340 --> 13:43.920
<b>so it rang a bell, that it did.</b>

13:46.340 --> 13:49.390
<b>You really do keep surprising me.</b>

13:50.760 --> 13:55.020
<b>Can you tell us the truth soon,
that is?</b>

13:56.440 --> 14:02.020
<b>The Takanis in the Aizu region were
a really famous family among doctors.</b>

14:02.860 --> 14:04.940
<b>The Takani family was an uncommon one,</b>

14:04.940 --> 14:08.030
<b>where women and children
also learned medicine.</b>

14:08.280 --> 14:11.450
<b>Despite the high standing
of being the Shogun's doctor,</b>

14:11.450 --> 14:15.750
<b>any sick person was treated with full
devotion, regardless of social position.</b>

14:17.250 --> 14:21.670
<b>For those of the samurai class who treat
social position as an absolute rule,</b>

14:21.670 --> 14:23.840
<b>they were despicable.</b>

14:23.840 --> 14:27.260
<b>But for us doctors,
they were our ideals in the flesh.</b>

14:28.010 --> 14:32.260
<b>Among them, Megumi's father
Ryusei Takani was at the pinnacle.</b>

14:32.720 --> 14:35.390
<b>As soon as he learned
how useful Dutch studies were,</b>

14:35.390 --> 14:36.850
<b>he immediately became lordless</b>

14:36.850 --> 14:40.310
<b>and took his entire family
to learn in Nagasaki.</b>

14:40.860 --> 14:43.860
<b>Just how much resolve
you needed to become lordless,</b>

14:43.860 --> 14:47.320
<b>young ones nowadays
can't possibly understand.</b>

14:47.820 --> 14:53.330
<b>The Takani family was given a special
exemption and returned to Aizu,</b>

14:53.330 --> 14:55.700
<b>but the Battle of Aizu
started at around the same time.</b>

14:56.700 --> 15:00.790
<b><i>The Battle of Aizu was the fourth battle
of the Boshin War,</i></b>

15:00.790 --> 15:04.500
<b><i>fought between the Aizu clan
and the Imperialist government army.</i></b>

15:05.050 --> 15:08.090
<b><i>The Aizu clan utilized everyone,
men and women, young and old,</i></b>

15:08.090 --> 15:09.590
<b><i>and even besieged their castle.</i></b>

15:09.590 --> 15:14.470
<b><i>But on September 22, 1868,
they surrendered.</i></b>

15:14.470 --> 15:18.600
<b><i>As the Aizu clan had protected Kyoto
before the Revolution</i></b>

15:18.600 --> 15:20.560
<b><i>and apprehended Imperialists,</i></b>

15:20.560 --> 15:24.860
<b><i>the members of the clan
were oppressed by the government</i></b>

15:24.860 --> 15:28.070
<b><i>for years on end since.</i></b>

15:28.740 --> 15:34.240
<b>The Takani family all headed out to war,
leaving a very young Megumi behind.</b>

15:34.240 --> 15:36.290
<b>As a result, Ryusei died in battle.</b>

15:36.290 --> 15:40.080
<b>Her mother and two older brothers
went missing in the flames of battle.</b>

15:40.660 --> 15:45.210
<b>And ever since,
Megumi has been all alone.</b>

15:46.800 --> 15:51.720
<b>She moved to Tokyo five years ago and
became assistant to a certain doctor.</b>

15:52.260 --> 15:56.930
<b>I was acquaintances with him,
so I came to know about Megumi back then.</b>

15:57.220 --> 16:03.900
<b>That doctor was murdered three years ago,
and she went missing at the same time.</b>

16:04.650 --> 16:06.900
<b>I definitely would love to meet Megumi.</b>

16:06.900 --> 16:08.360
<b>Where is she right now?</b>

16:08.610 --> 16:12.820
<b>Huh? Come to think of it,
I haven't seen her for a while now!</b>

16:12.820 --> 16:15.910
<b>Crap. Can she really have...</b>

16:17.030 --> 16:20.660
<b>I wasn't a great judge of character
five years ago.</b>

16:21.250 --> 16:23.960
<b>That doctor had secret ties with Kanryu.</b>

16:24.790 --> 16:29.000
<b>The doctor refined the opium ingredients
that Kanryu bought for cheap,</b>

16:29.000 --> 16:30.920
<b>and Kanryu then sold the refined drug.</b>

16:31.340 --> 16:33.470
<b>That's how things
were going well for them...</b>

16:34.300 --> 16:36.720
<b>until the doctor created this.</b>

16:37.640 --> 16:39.100
<b>It's called the Spiderweb.</b>

16:39.770 --> 16:41.310
<b>Its special refinement process</b>

16:41.310 --> 16:44.940
<b>needs only half the ingredients,
but doubles the dependency.</b>

16:45.440 --> 16:47.310
<b>So it quadruples the profits.</b>

16:47.900 --> 16:52.240
<b>If it seriously gets around, all of Tokyo
could be addicted to opium in five years.</b>

16:53.030 --> 16:54.410
<b>Kanryu sought mass distribution</b>

16:54.410 --> 16:57.530
<b>and tried to get the refinement process
out of the doctor.</b>

16:58.030 --> 17:01.450
<b>But the doctor kept his lips shut,
tried to monopolize the profits.</b>

17:02.040 --> 17:04.040
<b>There was a scuffle in due time,</b>

17:04.040 --> 17:07.080
<b>and Kanryu's group
accidentally killed the doctor.</b>

17:07.420 --> 17:11.670
<b>And I, as the only one who knew
how to refine it as his assistant,</b>

17:11.670 --> 17:13.760
<b>was forced to make it.</b>

17:15.630 --> 17:18.640
<b>When I learned that what I was creating</b>

17:18.640 --> 17:21.600
<b>was not medicine to save people,
but its reverse,</b>

17:21.600 --> 17:23.230
<b>I thought about dying.</b>

17:24.100 --> 17:26.730
<b>But I couldn't quite succeed at death.</b>

17:28.520 --> 17:33.110
<b>If I live and dabble in medicine,
someday I may be reunited</b>

17:33.110 --> 17:36.820
<b>with my mother or brothers
that I have been separated from.</b>

17:37.620 --> 17:39.990
<b>Thinking that, for the past three years,</b>

17:39.990 --> 17:42.950
<b>I kept making drugs
that drove people to death.</b>

17:47.290 --> 17:49.630
<b>So, Miss Megumi,
the reason why Kanryu is after you</b>

17:49.920 --> 17:53.960
<b>is because, to this day, nobody else
knows how to refine the drug, is it not?</b>

17:54.970 --> 17:59.800
<b>To curb production of Spiderweb and
minimize the number of its victims,</b>

17:59.800 --> 18:01.930
<b>you never let go of your guilt</b>

18:01.930 --> 18:04.980
<b>and decided to shoulder all of the burden
by yourself, did you not?</b>

18:06.270 --> 18:09.480
<b>If you agonized as such for three years,</b>

18:09.480 --> 18:12.860
<b>it's time for you to be forgiven
and be freed, that it is.</b>

18:14.280 --> 18:15.110
<b>Ken-san...</b>

18:16.240 --> 18:19.200
<b>There's no way they will back away
that easily, that there isn't.</b>

18:19.530 --> 18:22.410
<b>It's best if you stayed in the dojo
for a while longer, that it is.</b>

18:22.620 --> 18:23.870
<b>But...</b>

18:23.870 --> 18:26.000
<b>That's fine with you, Miss Kaoru?</b>

18:35.170 --> 18:38.930
<b>All right.
I know how hard it is to be all alone.</b>

18:39.760 --> 18:43.220
<b>I would be just like you
if Kenshin wasn't around.</b>

18:43.970 --> 18:47.270
<b>Finally, it's about how we deal
with Kanryu's group, that it is.</b>

18:49.060 --> 18:52.570
<b>But you better not make a move on Kenshin.</b>

18:52.570 --> 18:55.360
<b>I'll mercilessly toss you out
if that happens.</b>

19:03.410 --> 19:07.960
<b>I see. So Beshimi and Hyottoko
will be useless for a while.</b>

19:08.460 --> 19:09.370
<b>Yes, sir.</b>

19:09.540 --> 19:10.880
<b>So, Han'nya...</b>

19:11.580 --> 19:13.040
<b>what about your own wounds?</b>

19:13.540 --> 19:15.880
<b>Yes, though barely.</b>

19:16.550 --> 19:21.140
<b>As you mentioned,
that man was no ordinary man.</b>

19:21.430 --> 19:24.850
<b>I didn't expect him to take my hit</b>

19:24.850 --> 19:30.190
<b>and use that reaction
to try striking human vitals, the liver.</b>

19:31.230 --> 19:32.270
<b>Can you move?</b>

19:32.480 --> 19:35.270
<b>I cannot join combat
for two or three days,</b>

19:35.270 --> 19:36.780
<b>but if it's spy activities...</b>

19:37.280 --> 19:40.610
<b>All right. Dig up everything
about that man's past in three days.</b>

19:41.110 --> 19:42.110
<b>Yes, sir.</b>

19:44.410 --> 19:47.160
<b>Redhead, cross-shaped scar.</b>

19:48.120 --> 19:49.960
<b>So that man is indeed...</b>

21:33.850 --> 21:35.140
<b>What was that?</b>

21:35.140 --> 21:39.060
<b>He said, "Welcome,
the captain is waiting for you."</b>

21:39.060 --> 21:42.150
<b>Hmph. Quite a hospitable treatment.</b>

21:42.610 --> 21:45.780
<b>This truly is money doing the talking.</b>

21:56.250 --> 21:58.960
<b>So, Captain, what about those goods?</b>

22:07.380 --> 22:09.680
<b>Oh, is this it?</b>

22:21.570 --> 22:23.400
<b>With this, I will be invincible!</b>

22:23.900 --> 22:25.690
<b>Welcome to Japan!</b>

22:25.690 --> 22:28.360
<b>With this, I'm sure
everyone will grovel at my feet!</b>

22:28.820 --> 22:30.910
<b>And that's all thanks to money!</b>

22:30.910 --> 22:32.280
<b>The power money has!</b>

22:32.280 --> 22:35.580
<b>Oh, I'm so glad I am rich!</b>

22:45.090 --> 22:50.090
<b>NEXT EPISODE
A REASON TO ACT</b>

22:46.590 --> 22:49.220
<b><i>Next episode, "A Reason to Act."</i></b>
